    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `capacityWarning` field on `POST /api/owners`: it is `true` when the owner's city already holds **40\u201349** owners at creation time (approaching the limit), while the existing hard 409 rejection at 50 is untouched.\n\nFollowing the codebase's established pattern for derived warning flags (`bulkSignupWarning`, `possibleDuplicate`), the field is persisted on the owner and surfaced automatically via the OpenAPI-generated DTO + MapStruct name-matching:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `capacity_warning` column with getter/setter.\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean to the `Owner` response schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it; MapStruct maps it by name, no mapper edit needed).\n3. **Schema files** \u2014 added `capacity_warning BOOLEAN` to all four `db/*/schema.sql` files, and appended the matching `NULL` value to the 10 positional seed inserts in the hsqldb `data.sql` (the DB used by tests; h2/postgres use explicit column lists and were unaffected).\n4. **`FlagCapacityWarning.java`** (new) \u2014 counts existing owners in the built owner's city (same exact-city comparison as `RequireCityCapacity`, `findAll()`-iterate style like `FlagBulkSignup`) and sets `capacityWarning = count >= 40 && count < 50`, mutating the built owner in place before save.\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the `flagCapacityWarning` step into the pipeline under the write transaction, between `flagPossibleDuplicate` and `save` (after the hard-rejection `requireCityCapacity` step, so a count \u2265 50 never reaches it).\n\nTest result: `AcceptanceTest.coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` passes and the full suite reports **BUILD SUCCESS** (1 test, 0 failures/errors).",
